# Garelier nested .gitignore (v2.5.0) — lives at __garelier/.gitignore
#
# DEC-051: Garelier never edits the project's ROOT .gitignore. These rules live
# inside __garelier/ (the only tree Garelier owns). git honors nested .gitignore
# files, so every pattern below is RELATIVE TO __garelier/ and applies to every
# <pm_id> directory under it. The project root stays pristine and removable —
# delete __garelier/ and this file goes with it. No churn lands on the project's
# own .gitignore as the framework evolves.

# Runtime state directory (transient; never tracked)
# Includes runtime/driver/ for autonomous mode pid files and logs.
*/runtime/

# W-091: a hook that mis-anchors its state (a cwd-relative fallback, a wrong
# pm_id) can drop a `.claude/runtime/` tree anywhere UNDER __garelier/ — deeper
# than the `*/runtime/` rule above reaches. That state is transient like
# runtime/; never track it, wherever under __garelier/ it lands (defence-in-depth
# behind the hook's own root-anchor fix).
**/.claude/runtime/

# Worktree containers (managed by `git worktree`, not tracked content)
*/_workers/
*/_scouts/
*/_smiths/
*/_librarians/
*/_observers/
*/_artisan/
*/_guardians/
*/_concierges/

# DEC-063/065 ephemeral producer homes: each _dispatch<N>/ holds a STATE.md and a
# checkout/ worktree, created by dispatch_prepare and removed by dispatch_cleanup.
# Transient like runtime/ — never tracked.
*/_dispatch*/

# DEC-076 Wanderer: an external advisory peer (separately-launched Codex/Claude,
# no lane/branch). It creates NO container today; reserved so any future per-
# Wanderer home is ignored like the other role containers.
*/_wanderers/

# Dock's working directory (transient state only)
*/_dock/

# PM's role identity file (other <pm_id>/_pm/ files are tracked deliverables)
*/_pm/CLAUDE.md

# W-086 layout v2 (_crew): role containers collapse one level under _crew/. Both
# the flat (pre-v2) patterns above and the _crew/ (v2) patterns below are kept so
# a mixed, un-migrated, or freshly-migrated install stays covered either way. Note
# _crew/pm/ holds TRACKED deliverables (history.md, setup_config.toml) — only its
# CLAUDE.md is ignored, exactly as for the flat _pm/.
*/_crew/workers/
*/_crew/scouts/
*/_crew/smiths/
*/_crew/librarians/
*/_crew/observers/
*/_crew/artisan/
*/_crew/guardians/
*/_crew/concierges/
*/_crew/dispatch*/
*/_crew/wanderers/
*/_crew/dock/
*/_crew/pm/CLAUDE.md

# W-085 showcase: the default drop-zone for user-facing deliverables (screenshots,
# audio previews). Transient like runtime/ — never tracked. Curated keepers are
# promoted to gallery/ (tracked, LFS), which is re-included below.
*/showcase/

# DEC-020: worktree roles keep their git worktree in a `checkout/` subdir, so
# coordination files (STATE.md, assignment.md, report.md, …) live in the
# container — already covered by the `*/_workers/` … `*/_artisan/` rules above —
# and never appear inside a worktree.

# Re-include the persistent control documents
!*/control/
!*/control/**

# DEC-077 two-layer knowledge model: knowledge is authority like control/ and is
# TRACKED, never ignored. SHARED layer = __atmos/knowledge/ (general __atmos tier,
# a sibling of the <pm_id>/ dirs); PER-PM layer = <pm_id>/knowledge/. Re-include
# both explicitly so no present-or-future ignore rule can swallow them.
!__atmos/
!__atmos/**
!*/knowledge/
!*/knowledge/**

# W-085 gallery: curated user-facing keepers, TRACKED (binaries via Git LFS).
# Re-included explicitly so no present-or-future ignore rule can swallow it.
!*/gallery/
!*/gallery/**

# Local backups
*.bak
*.bak.*
